<article class="env-lemma" id="01PU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01PU">Lemma <span data-tag="01PU">28.27.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an ample invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. For any closed subscheme $Z \subset X$ the restriction of $\mathcal{L}$ to $Z$ is ample. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear since a closed subset of a quasi-compact space is quasi-compact and a closed subscheme of an affine scheme is affine (see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01IH" data-tag="01IH">26.8.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>